{"chunk_id": "3346904981dc", "text": "Indrajit boasts before the court of Lanka of his past victories over the gods, recalling how even Indra\u2019s elephant Airavata fell before his might. In response, Vibhishana rebukes the prince sharply, calling his arrogance childish and warning that Rama\u2019s arrows are as irresistible as the rod of Brahma or Yama\u2019s sceptre. He urges the only prudent course: return Sita to Rama with gifts and avert destruction. Ravana reacts with fury, declaring that treacherous relatives are worse than open enemies and accusing Vibhishana of disloyalty. He compares kin to hidden betrayers who deliver their own kind to danger. Insulted yet respectful, Vibhishana rises into the air with his followers, condemning Ravana\u2019s loss of judgment\u2014an early step toward his break with Lanka.\nRavana angrily denounces Vibhishana\u2019s counsel to return Sita, accusing him of treachery, prompting Vibhishana to depart in indignation.\nThemes: loyalty vs righteousness, family conflict, hubris, counsel rejected, moral duty", "vector": [-0.006652642972767353, -0.02564891055226326, 0.006645774003118277, 0.014699696563184261, 0.005488344933837652, 0.012721420265734196, -0.03104795701801777, -0.020538361743092537, -0.01655433140695095, -0.012570301070809364, 0.01279010996222496, -0.012556563131511211, 0.020236125215888023, -0.0025157774798572063, -0.012913752347230911, -0.0016854851273819804, 0.04448375478386879, -0.01262525375932455, 0.03992272913455963, -0.01611471362411976, -0.006978921592235565, -0.005206714849919081, -0.011052248999476433, 0.006281716283410788, -0.03319109231233597, 0.005385309457778931, 0.024041559547185898, -0.026280859485268593, 0.014232603833079338, -0.009128923527896404, -0.007604002021253109, -0.01311295386403799, 0.019508007913827896, 0.0014175934484228492, -0.030855625867843628, -0.008496974594891071, -0.009747135452926159, -0.015551455318927765, 0.026734214276075363, -0.0010827288497239351, 0.011059117503464222, -0.01